15. (Currently amended) A method for selecting an edge server computer from a plurality of server computers for sending data to a client computer, the method comprising the steps of:
accessing a server computer through a path in a computer network, the path including one or more server computers;
adding information indicative of at least one server computer of the first set of one or more server computers to a locator of a resource on the second server computer, __wherein the information includes data regarding server load, latency, or geographic proximity__;
the resource having a unique signature as part of its identifier; and
selecting the first server computer based on the information added to the locator, __wherein the selection is performed by a media request broker that receives the locator from the client computer and determines the first server computer prior to establishing a connection between the client computer and the first server computer__.

16. (Currently amended) The method of claim 15, __wherein the second server computer is a Web application server comprising a Web page with a hyperlink referencing the data to be sent to the client computer, the hyperlink including a unique signature, and wherein the method further comprises the steps of: selecting the hyperlink by the client computer; generating an http request out of the hyperlink by a web browser, the http request containing the unique signature identifying a media request; transmitting the http request to the media request broker; and the media request broker selecting the first server computer based on the unique signature and the information added to the locator__.

